WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.319
Week 31: Comparison, Register, and Idiomatic Force. make a nuanced comparison praise or criticize appropriately interpret idioms from context

2
00:00:10.319 --> 00:00:23.820
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Use más/menos + adjective + que for comparisons, el/la más + adjective for superlatives, and tan + adjective + como for equality.

3
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:50.569
Model set. Esta opción es mucho más eficiente que la anterior. Es la propuesta menos clara de todas. Es tan buena como esperábamos. Es, con diferencia, la mejor opción. El proyecto mejoró notablemente. This option is much more efficient than the previous one. It's the least clear proposal of all. It's as good as we expected. It's by far the best option. The project improved notably.

4
00:00:50.569 --> 00:01:00.699
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:14.754
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: make a nuanced comparison; praise or criticize appropriately; interpret idioms from context. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:14.754 --> 00:01:42.356
Model language. Esta opción es mucho más eficiente que la anterior. — This option is much more efficient than the previous one. Es la propuesta menos clara de todas. — It's the least clear proposal of all. Es tan buena como esperábamos. — It's as good as we expected. Es, con diferencia, la mejor opción. — It's by far the best option. El proyecto mejoró notablemente. — The project improved notably.

7
00:01:42.356 --> 00:01:52.105
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
